<Base title="Privacy" description="How StatusGrid handles URL lists and checker results."><section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span><h1>Your working list stays yours.</h1><p>A plain-language overview of data used by the checker.</p></div></section><section class="content-section"><div class="container prose"><h2>URL checks</h2><p>When you run a check, the URL list is sent to the StatusGrid server so it can request those public pages. The checked websites can see a request from the server. Results are returned to your browser; the app does not create an account or save reports in a database.</p><h2>Files and exports</h2><p>TXT and CSV imports are read in your browser to populate the input. Only the URLs you choose to check are sent to the server. CSV exports are generated in your browser.</p><h2>Operational logs</h2><p>Your hosting provider or reverse proxy may keep ordinary access logs, including IP addresses, timestamps, and request metadata. Their retention depends on the deployment configuration.</p></div></section></Base>
